# SQL's uppercase `LIMIT`: DS0105. `limit` itself is accepted.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | LIMIT 10
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..24
  PIPELINE@0..23
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    TAKE_OP@15..23
      IDENT@15..20 "LIMIT"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      LITERAL@21..23
        LONG@21..23 "10"
  WHITESPACE@23..24 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `LIMIT` is not an operator
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | LIMIT 10
  |                ^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: operator names are lowercase: write `limit`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | limit 10
which parses without errors
